<p class="close-kicker">Question 4</p>
<h1 class="slide-q">Do young players get ice time at home?</h1>
<p class="slide-a">{% if q4.home.mean_u21_games_share < q4.peers.Liiga.mean_u21_games_share and q4.home.mean_u21_games_share < q4.peers.SHL.mean_u21_games_share %}Less than in Finland and Sweden.{% else %}About as much as in Finland and Sweden.{% endif %} Under-21 skaters play <strong>{{ pct(q4.home.mean_u21_games_share) }} of Extraliga games</strong> and {{ pct(q4.home.mean_u21_toi_share) }} of its ice time; the Liiga gives them {{ pct(q4.peers.Liiga.mean_u21_games_share) }} and {{ pct(q4.peers.Liiga.mean_u21_toi_share) }}, the SHL {{ pct(q4.peers.SHL.mean_u21_games_share) }} and {{ pct(q4.peers.SHL.mean_u21_toi_share) }}.</p>
<figure class="figure-bleed" data-chart="q4-youth">
  <table class="fig-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">League</th><th scope="col" class="num">Under-21 share of games</th><th scope="col" class="num">of ice time</th><th scope="col" class="num">Seasons measured</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="is-home"><td>Extraliga</td><td class="num">{{ pct(q4.home.mean_u21_games_share) }}</td><td class="num">{{ pct(q4.home.mean_u21_toi_share) }}</td><td class="num">{{ q4.home.measured_seasons }}</td></tr>
      {% for name, s in q4.peers.items() %}<tr><td>{{ name }}</td><td class="num">{{ pct(s.mean_u21_games_share) }}</td><td class="num">{{ pct(s.mean_u21_toi_share) }}</td><td class="num">{{ s.measured_seasons }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <figcaption>How to read it: the share of all skater games (or of skater ice time) played by skaters aged 20 or less, season by season over {{ q4.window }}. The Extraliga is blue, the Liiga ink, the SHL grey. The National League and the DEL are dashed and marked "not measured": they publish no birth dates, so ages are known for only about {{ pct0(q4.unmeasured_known.NL) }} and {{ pct0(q4.unmeasured_known.DEL) }} of their games, and their shares only count the young players who could be linked to another league.</figcaption>
</figure>
<details class="fold slide-method" open>
  <summary>How we know</summary>
  <p class="slide-did"><span class="slide-did-label">What we did</span> Every skater of every nationality, regular season. A league-season counts as measured when ages are known for at least 90% of its skater games; the Extraliga, Liiga and SHL are measured in all {{ q4.n_seasons }} seasons. Ice time is published by the Extraliga from 2013/14, the Liiga from 2014/15 and the SHL from 2009/10. Goalkeepers are in <a href="{{ prefix }}{{ qurl.q7 }}">question 7</a>.</p>
  <p class="slide-how"><span class="slide-how-label">Ratios</span> The Extraliga's under-21 share of games is {{ f2(q4.comparison.Liiga.games_share_ratio_home_to_league) }} times the Liiga's and {{ f2(q4.comparison.SHL.games_share_ratio_home_to_league) }} times the SHL's; of ice time, {{ f2(q4.comparison.Liiga.toi_share_ratio_home_to_league) }} and {{ f2(q4.comparison.SHL.toi_share_ratio_home_to_league) }}. In {{ q4.latest_season }} the Extraliga share was {{ pct(q4.home.latest.u21_games_share) }} of games and {{ pct(q4.home.latest.u21_toi_share) }} of ice time.</p>
</details>
